      "text": "A database needs an index to make searching faster. Imagine you have a huge library of books, and you want to find a specific book. An index is like a map that tells you where each book is located. Instead of going through every book, you can go straight to the one you want.\n\nOne benefit of an index is that it speeds up search times, making the database more efficient.\n\nOne tradeoff is that indexes take up extra space and slow down updates. When you add, change, or delete data, the index must also be updated, which can be time-consuming, especially for large databases.",
