      "text": "1. **Data Requirements**: Training requires a large amount of labeled data to teach the model, while inference can be done with minimal or no labeled data, as the model uses previously learned patterns.\n\n2. **Resource Usage**: Training involves significant computational resources, such as GPUs or TPUs, to optimize the model's performance. Inference, in contrast, is computationally lighter and can be performed on standard hardware.\n\n3. **Model Complexity**: Training often involves more complex models with more parameters, which requires more time and resources. Inference typically uses simpler models with fewer parameters, making it faster and more efficient.",
